i.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm generally not a fan of the conduct around builtin scripts. We can't keep stacking hacks, at least not if a lot of people seem to be quite attached to the feature and don't want it to be removed in favor of streamlining GDScript.\n\nThere is another more concrete issue I take with this PR: The GDScript implementation of `get_classes_used` relies on `ResourceLoader::load` to process the received path. As such passing a builtin path to it is subject to the cold loading issues described in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116593\nI'm not deeply familiar with the resource loader, but afaik there is no guarantee that the resource was already loaded prior. Am I wrong about this?\n","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119413#pullrequestreview-4298567361","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119413","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119413#pullrequestreview-4298567361"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119413"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-15T1